        "id": 1066075
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-03-16T13:18:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "AFAICT this method uses in-band signaling to tell whether a path is:\n\n- A Soong output path (if it starts with out/soong)\n- An output path (if it starts with out/)\n- A source path (anything else)\n\nAn alternative would be to use out-of-band signaling and have assertion methods like\n\nAssertSourcePath(...)\nAssertOutPath(...)\nAssertSoongOutPath(...)\n\nIt would look a bit nicer (in-band signaling is icky because what if e.g. you have out/Android.bp), but:\n\n- You\u0027d need a 3x more assertion methods\n- The cases where you currently pass a []string as a set of expected paths would become complicated if you want to pass in a mixture of source and output paths.\n\nIs this similar to your reasons for choosing in-band signaling here?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 896,
        "startChar": 5,
        "endLine": 896,
        "endChar": 28
      },
      "revId": "567465da8cf04b436e82be5c0f2fa46f0f2001aa",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d75ba158_7934657a",
        "filename": "android/testing.go",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 896,
      "author": {
        "id": 1039338
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-03-16T13:33:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I can\u0027t say that I thought of all those issues with \"out-of-band\" signalling but definitely some of them were a factor, e.g. number of assertion methods, mixture of path types, etc.\n\nOne reason that is missing is that a lot of tests are data driven and provide a list of expected paths, some of those are mixtures. Handling them this way would be complicated.\n\nAnother reason was to keep the size of the changes down.\n\n\"out/Android.bp\" should not be a problem because it is impossible to create such a file in the real build because it ensures that source and output directories do not overlap.\n\nIn tests the sources are in the mock file system and outputs are in the real file system so they can never overlap. However, it would be possible to add \"out/Android.bp\" to a test fixture and so I will add a check in the fixture to prevent anyone adding anything to \"out/\".",
      "parentUuid": "5980f074_beee178f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 896,
        "startChar": 5,
        "endLine": 896,
        "endChar": 28
      },
      "revId": "567465da8cf04b436e82be5c0f2fa46f0f2001aa",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
